                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, light armour and a shield. May have heavy armour (+4 pts), throwing or thrusting spear (+2 pts), and either javelins (+2 pts) or a bow (+3 pts). If on foot, he may have a double-handed weapon (+2 pts), an additional hand weapon (+3 pts) or a Dane Axe (+2 pts). May ride a warhorse (+16 pts). Army General Options: if no other General has been chosen, a Voevodo may be upgraded to Army General (+25 pts). (Byzantium p.88)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="233d-dd46-cc5c-830f" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="4+">
                <conditions>
                <condition field="selections" scope="ea79-b7ee-b813-7006" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="ebd0-ddc5-cc5c-f355" type="atLeast"/>
