  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="6349-3a0c-13ff-2a24" name="Rus (Byzantium) - List Notes" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false">
      <description>RUS (Byzantium: Beyond the Golden Gate, pp.85-89): armies of the Pagan Rus, the Rus Princes, the Great Rus and the Rus of the Mongol Invasion, 750-1250 AD. Special rule: Dane Axes - the smaller one-handed axes are hand weapons; the one-and-half axes are Dane Axes which count as halberds; the great or double-handed axes follow the rules for normal double-handed weapons (a halberd or other two-handed weapon cannot use armour save other than a shield).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Rus - Early Pagan Rus]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Cavalry: up to 0%
  EARLY PAGAN RUS (750-950 AD). An Army General is required (Warlord: must contain a unit of Varjazi). Characters up to 25%; Cavalry none; Infantry at least 25%; at least one unit of Varjazi must be chosen (not enforced); Allies up to 25% (documented only).
[Rus - Era of the Princes]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  ERA OF THE PRINCES (950-1100 AD). An Army General is required. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry at least 25% (no Grid Druzhina or Chernye Klobuki); Infantry any; Allies up to 25% (documented only).
[Rus - Great Rus]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  GREAT RUS (1100-1200 AD). An Army General is required. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry at least 50%; Infantry up to 50%; Allies up to 25% (documented only). Malaia Druzhina may have warhorses (+3 pts per model).
[Rus - Mongol Invasion]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  MONGOL INVASION (1200-1250 AD). An Army General is required. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry at least 50%; Infantry up to 50% (no Varjazi, Smerd or Voi); Allies up to 25% (documented only). Malaia Druzhina may have warhorses (+3 pts per model). Rus Skirmishers may take crossbows (+4 pts) and light armour (+2 pts).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
